@startuml digital-product-purchase
skinparam defaultFontName Helvetica
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundCorner 8
skinparam ArrowColor #666666
skinparam ArrowFontColor #666666
skinparam wrapWidth 200
skinparam maxMessageSize 160
title Digital product purchase, license retrieval and activation report
autonumber

actor "Client application" as client
participant "Purchase Coordinator" as coordinator
participant "Inventory Service" as inventory
participant "Payment Service" as payment
participant "License Service" as license

client -> coordinator: POST /purchases\n(productId, customerId, authorized amount/currency, paymentToken)
note over client,coordinator: Stable purchase key; the coordinator assigns one purchaseId.\nfulfil-purchase runs inside this exchange before its response.
group fulfil-purchase / reserve-and-capture
coordinator -> inventory: POST /reservations\n(productId, quantity: 1)
inventory --> coordinator: 201 (reservationId, current amount/currency, RESERVED)
note over coordinator,inventory: Compare product, amount and currency with customer authorization.\nMismatch stops payment and issuance.
coordinator -> payment: POST /captures\n(reservationId, amountMinor, currency, paymentToken)
payment --> coordinator: 200 (paymentId, actual capture state) or uncertainty
note over coordinator,payment: Only matching CAPTURED evidence allows continuation.\nDECLINED or UNKNOWN stops issuance; reconcile the original attempt.
end

group fulfil-purchase / issue-license (eligible path only)
coordinator -> license: POST /licenses\n(purchaseId, customerId, productId, reservationId, paymentId)
license --> coordinator: 201 (licenseId, purchaseId, READY)
note over coordinator,license: One license for the original issuance key.\nPersist the scoped purchase/license before confirming the client.
end
coordinator --> client: 201 (purchaseId, licenseId, READY) only after confirmed fulfilment

client -> coordinator: GET /purchases/{purchaseId}/bundle?deviceId=...
note over client,coordinator: Check customer ownership and READY state; bind material to this device.
coordinator --> client: 200 (licenseId, protectedBundle, deviceId, READY)
note over client: Device attempts activation outside this HTTP workflow.
client -> coordinator: POST /purchases/{purchaseId}/activation-events\n(licenseId, deviceId, ACTIVATED or FAILED)
coordinator --> client: 204 (event received)
note over client,coordinator: Receipt acknowledgement does not assert activation success.\nFailure follow-up is outside this small example.
@enduml
